# Lorenz's equations of 1963, nine years too late for Whirlwind:
#   x' = s(y - x),  y' = x(r - z) - y,  z' = xy - bz,
# with s = 10, r = 28, b = 8/3, from (1, 1, 1). The path wanders between two
# lobes, x positive and x negative. Printed every quarter of a unit to t = 3.
    t = 0,
    h = 0.01,
    s = 10, r = 28, b = 8/3,
    x = 1, y = 1, z = 1,
1   PRINT t, x, y, z.
    n = 0,
2   Dx = s(y - x),
    Dy = x(r - z) - y,
    Dz = xy - bz,
    n = n + 1,
    e = n - 24.5,
    CP 2,
    e = t - 2.995,
    CP 1,
    STOP
